# Bot1 has Rest in Peace out on turn 1; Bot2 has two Islands and Counterspell by turn 5. There Faithless Looting makes
# Bot1 discard Basking Rootwalla and a Mountain; Bot1 orders madness first (CR 616.1), so the Rootwalla is exiled and
# its trigger lets Bot1 cast it for {0} (CR 702.35a). It is a spell like any other (the madness rulings): Bot2 counters
# it, and the countered card's move to the graveyard is an ordinary one that Rest in Peace exiles - madness applies only
# to a discard. Counterspell is exiled after it resolves too.

